  "problem": "Which number corresponds to the midpoint of the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB},$ if $A$ and $B$ are points on a number line that correspond to $-4$ and $2$, respectively?",
  "worked_solution": "The point $A$ corresponds to the number ${x}_{1}=-4$ while $B$ corresponds to ${x}_{2}=2.$ \n\nTo find the number ${x}_{m}$ corresponding to the midpoint $M$, we use the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{m} & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+2}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14171842/assets/eaf87888628f29d0025632a98df3d778307b1cfdb4538d997529db13c8518aba.png)",
